# --- OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
venv/
.venv/
env/
.ruff_cache/
# unsloth codegens patched trainer sources into cwd on import; 3.4 MB, regenerable
unsloth_compiled_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- the resolved environment, not the spec (recreate with pip install -r requirements.txt)
requirements.lock.txt

# --- model weights and quantized artefacts: large, and regenerable from adapter + base
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.bin
*.pt
*.ckpt
outputs/
adapters/
merged/
hf_cache/
runs/

# --- data is append-only and large; it lives on disk, never in git.
# The directory shapes are tracked via .gitkeep, the contents never are.
data/raw/*
data/interim/*
data/processed/*
!data/**/.gitkeep

# --- adapters are tens of MB and regenerable from config + data; merged models never.
checkpoints/*
!checkpoints/.gitkeep

# --- scratch only, never canonical
notebooks/*
!notebooks/.gitkeep

# --- run artefacts
wandb/
*.log

# --- trainwatch runtime state ------------------------------------------------
# STILL LIVE after step 6. The package left this repo; its state did not. The
# SQLite store, its WAL, heartbeats and hub blobs are machine-local and
# per-box: the trainer and `scripts/trainwatch serve` share one DB file on the
# machine doing the training. Never committed.
var/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Anchored to the repo root. This was `heartbeat*`, which is unanchored and so
# matched at EVERY level -- including src/trainwatch/heartbeat.py, a source
# module that src/trainwatch/__init__.py imports. That file was therefore never
# committed, and `import src.trainwatch` failed on any fresh clone. Nothing
# caught it because nobody had cloned fresh; CI found it on its first run.
# (Those two modules left in step 6; the anchoring is kept because the failure
# mode is a property of the pattern, not of the package that exposed it.)
#
# It was also redundant: the heartbeat file lives at var/heartbeat, and var/ is
# already ignored two lines above. Kept anchored anyway, for a heartbeat file
# written to the repo root by an explicit TRAINWATCH_HEARTBEAT.
/heartbeat*
logs/
.env
.env.local
*.key

# --- the dashboard's ignores are gone, deliberately --------------------------
# dashboard/node_modules/, dashboard/dist/ and dashboard/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
# were here until step 6 deleted dashboard/. An ignore for a path that cannot
# exist hides nothing and tells the next reader this repo still has a Node
# workspace. It does not: the dashboard, its build and the committed bundle at
# src/trainwatch/server/static/ all live in Platform now and ship inside the
# installed trainwatch distribution.


# --- tooling caches ---------------------------------------------------------
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   configs/     -- configs/ IS the lab notebook. A config that is not committed did not happen.
#   results/     -- written by hand, one markdown file per phase. Your future self reads only this.
#   data/tasks/  -- eval fixtures are .jsonl and MUST be versioned. A blanket data/**/*.jsonl
#                   rule would silently swallow them, so the data rules above are scoped to
#                   raw/ interim/ processed/ only. Verified 2026-09-17:
#                   `git check-ignore -v data/tasks/dev.jsonl` matches nothing, so this
#                   scoping does work and always did.
#
#                   What did NOT work: there were no fixtures. The directory was empty
#                   and, having no .gitkeep, was not tracked either -- so a fresh clone
#                   got no data/tasks/ at all, and BUILDING-ULTRON.md:920's "write ~20
#                   problems to data/tasks/dev.jsonl" failed on a path that did not
#                   exist. An audit read this comment, saw "MUST be versioned" next to
#                   nothing versioned, and concluded the rules above were swallowing
#                   them. They were not; the fixtures had never been written. A stated
#                   invariant with no instance of itself is indistinguishable from a
#                   broken rule, which is why the marker below now exists.
#
#                   data/tasks/.gitkeep pins the shape. It does not make the fixtures
#                   exist -- nothing can -- but a fresh clone now has the directory the
#                   guide tells you to write into, and this comment is no longer the
#                   only evidence that it is meant to be tracked.
#
# Removed from this list in step 6, because both paths were deleted:
#   src/trainwatch/server/static/  the BUILT dashboard, committed so the
#                   training box never needed Node.
#   dashboard/      the dashboard SOURCE.
# Both are Platform's now. The built bundle ships inside the installed
# trainwatch distribution, so the training box still never needs Node.
